# about AI crawlers, which do not index — they ingest — so the directive they
# read is Disallow, and until 2026-09-12 ai.txt handed them a blanket
# "Allow: /en-us/" that explicitly covered this page.
#
# THIS BLOCK REPEATS THE GLOBAL RULES ON PURPOSE. In robots.txt a named
# user-agent group REPLACES the "*" group for that crawler — it does not
# inherit from it. Listing only the Disallow below would have silently handed
# these bots /api/, /sign-in and the rest.
#
# AND THE "*" GROUP DELIBERATELY DOES NOT GET THIS ENTRY. A Disallow stops the
# crawl, so Googlebot would never fetch the page and never read the noindex
# that de-indexes it — a blocked URL can still surface as a bare link. Disallow
# and noindex are alternatives, not layers; see the note above this function.
# Each is aimed at the crawler it actually works on.
